  "rationale": "structural: The requirement is about what the skill document tells agents to do. The root `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is the skill text, so it is the artifact the requirement governs. It has no code structure to check, such as libraries, types, signatures or delegation. Each clause is a content obligation on that file, and the file meets each one in the Workflow step 2 paragraph (`section[Habeas%20requirements]/section[Workflow]/paragraph@c9eb6f7295df`):\n- It says to write drafts \"as uncommitted, unstaged edits, with no draft marker\".\n- It says to add a new chapter \"to `SUMMARY.md` and `git add -N` it\".\n\nI found no structural obligation that lacks evidence.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement obliges the `habeas-requirements` skill to direct agents to do three things: (a) write drafts as uncommitted, unstaged edits to the book; (b) leave no draft marker; and (c) for a new chapter, add it to `SUMMARY.md` and record it with `git add -N`. The requirement has no modes or boundaries.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_writes_drafts_as_unstaged_edits_without_markers]` covers all three:\n- It finds the numbered workflow step containing \"Write drafts\" with `step_of`. It takes that step's text with `step`, which uses `workflow_steps` to collapse wrapped lines.\n- It then uses `assert_text`, which asserts `contains` for each phrase.\n- The phrase \"Write drafts from the request straight into the chapter as uncommitted, unstaged edits, with no draft marker\" covers (a) and (b).\n- The phrase \"For a new chapter, add it to `SUMMARY.md` and `git add -N` it\" covers (c).\n\nThe bundled skill text in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` step 2 contains both phrases once whitespace is collapsed. The test would fail if either instruction were dropped or reworded. No obligation is untested.",
